\begin{proof}
\uses{limits-remark-finite-type-gives-well-defined-system, limits-lemma-proper-limit-of-proper-finite-presentation, limits-lemma-descend-finite-presentation, limits-lemma-eventually-proper}

By the discussion in
Remark \ref{limits-remark-finite-type-gives-well-defined-system}
the choice of $i_1$ and $W$ fitting into a diagram as in
(\ref{equation-good-diagram}) is immaterial for the truth of
the lemma. Thus we choose $W$ as follows.
First we choose a closed immersion $X \to X'$
with $X' \to S$ proper and of finite presentation, see
